      "raw_description": "Company Description: Amoh is a medical AI research lab focused on developing reinforcement-learning environments and datasets that simulate real clinical work. The lab builds systems where models are trained and evaluated against actual clinical outcomes, enabling robust assessment of AI performance in healthcare tasks. Amoh’s mission is to advance safe, effective AI tools that can support clinicians in real-world decision-making. Team members collaborate across AI research, healthcare, and data engineering to create scalable solutions for clinical practice. Role Description: The Artificial Intelligence Research Intern will contribute to the design and implementation of evaluations and RL environments for training AI models for clinical and medical tasks. Day-to-day responsibilities include exploring research literature, developing task sets, exploring a vast amount of clinical data, writing clean and efficient code, running and analyzing experimental results, and preparing reports on findings. The intern will collaborate with researchers and engineers to build datasets, evaluations, and tools around evaluations for clinical AI systems. Qualifications Strong foundation in Computer Science, including data structures, algorithms, models, and systems relevant to AI research. Programming skills in languages commonly used in AI research (e.g., Python), and familiarity with machine learning frameworks. Demonstrated Research skills, such as literature review, experimental design, and clear documentation of results. Ability to work occasionally on-site in Bengaluru, in a hybrid setting, collaborate in a multidisciplinary team, and communicate technical ideas effectively. Interest in medical AI, healthcare applications, and ethical considerations in clinical decision-support systems.",
