      "description": "About SmartQ: SmartQ is redefining how the world experiences food. As a next-generation food-tech innovator, we solve real operational challenges through empathy-led insights and powerful technology. Our mission is clear: to elevate everyday dining into a seamless and meaningful ...",
      "raw_description": "About SmartQ: SmartQ is redefining how the world experiences food. As a next-generation food-tech innovator, we solve real operational challenges through empathy-led insights and powerful technology. Our mission is clear: to elevate everyday dining into a seamless and meaningful experience. In the last decade, we’ve transformed cafeteria and food operations across industries with scalable, cutting-edge solutions. Operating in 14 countries and backed by Compass Group- a $60B global foodservice leader SmartQ continues to push the boundaries of what modern food-tech can achieve. Since our inception in 2015, we’ve become a trusted partner for corporates, hospitals, universities, and food courts worldwide. With a bold vision to become the world’s largest B2B food-tech company, we connect people through exceptional food experiences powered by advanced technology. Today, we proudly serve 400+ global clients, including leaders like Google, HSBC, Amazon, and Wells Fargo. At the heart of SmartQ is a culture shaped by four core pillars: Great People | Great Food | Great Experience | Greater Good These values inspire collaboration, innovation, humility, and a relentless pursuit of excellence. To dive deeper into what drives us, explore our cultural pillars on the SmartQ LinkedIn ‘Life’ page. It offers an authentic glimpse into the journey you could be part of: https://www.linkedin.com/company/smartq-bottlelabs/life/cdc290f8-ff81-4e7f-9c96-37d842f936c4/?viewA… Are you excited to join our team as Associate Product Manager? We are looking for a motivated, result-oriented and who is passionate about solving real-world business and user problems through technology and design. In this role, you will take ownership of key product areas, collaborate with cross-functional teams, and translate customer insights and business requirements into scalable product solutions. You will work closely with engineering, design, and business teams to drive product development, ensure seamless execution, and deliver impactful solutions. If you are enthusiastic about building innovative products and making a difference in the food-tech industry, we would love to have you on our team! Roles and responsibilities: Solutioning: Translate business challenges and requirements into well-defined product solutions, outlining scope, possible approaches, dependencies, and edge cases. Product Discovery: Drive product discovery through user research, market analysis, competitor benchmarking, and customer insights to identify opportunities and shape product strategy. Product Documentation: Create and maintain product documentation, including Product Requirement Documents (PRDs), user stories, acceptance criteria, release notes Technical Collaboration: Work closely with engineering teams to assess technical feasibility, understand dependencies, evaluate effort estimates Design Collaboration: Partner with UI/UX teams to develop wireframes and mock-ups using tools such as Figma, ensuring designs align with business and product requirements. Cross-functional Coordination: Collaborate with engineering, design, business, and customer success teams to ensure smooth product execution and delivery. Product Performance: Monitor product performance through customer feedback, and data analysis to identify improvement opportunities and drive continuous enhancement. Agile Product Management: Participate in sprint planning, backlog grooming, sprint reviews, and release management while promoting Agile best practices. Delivery Management: Track product features throughout development, testing, and deployment, proactively follow up on dependencies and blockers, and provide regular progress updates to stakeholders Qualifications: 1+ year of experience in Product Management, preferably within a B2B technology environment. Bachelor's degree in a relevant field. Experience in contributing to product launches, feature development, and product enhancements. Strong stakeholder management and cross-functional collaboration skills. Analytical mindset with hands-on experience in working with data, KPIs, metrics, and OKRs. Familiarity with product discovery methodologies, user research, and market analysis. Understanding of wireframing and prototyping, with exposure to tools such as Figma. Experience in creating PRDs, user stories, Jira tickets, and acceptance criteria. Good understanding of Agile methodologies, sprint planning, and product lifecycle management. Ability to understand technical concepts and collaborate effectively with engineering teams. Excellent communication, problem-solving, and presentation skills, with the ability to engage technical and non-technical stakeholders. Self-driven, adaptable, detail-oriented, and comfortable working in a fast-paced and dynamic environment. Message from CEO: Food is an everyday necessity, but the experience around it can influence how we feel, connect, and go about our day. At SmartQ, we see an opportunity to make these everyday moments better, one meal at a time. Our aggregation model, powered by technology and operational excellence, brings together food partners, processes, and people to transform dining experience. By combining these capabilities, we continuously seek better ways to solve problems, improve efficiency, and create experiences that are simpler, smarter, and more human. As we continue to redefine this space, we believe the next breakthrough can come from anyone who questions convention, sees possibilities where others see routine, and brings a fresh perspective to a familiar challenge. We look forward to welcoming minds who will challenge our thinking and help shape what SmartQ becomes next. We invite you to be that person. Together, let’s make everyday experiences extraordinary.",
